// switch-tap-echo: --buffer 1024
// tolerance_usecs: 4000
// The peer holds its receive window at zero, so the first 1024-byte echo fills
// Switch's tx buffer and later in-order segments remain unread. Switch advertises
// its 1024-byte receive window target throughout, independent of those held frames.
// Each full-window segment triggers an immediate window-update ACK. The peer's
// probe gets an ACK, then opening its window lets every queued echo drain.
// The handshake ACK comes 100 ms after the SYN-ACK: that RTT sample makes
// switch's RTO 100 + 4 * 50 = 300 ms, so the zero-window probe the first echo
// arms at 1.2 s is due at 1.5 s. The peer opens at 1.46 s, before it.

